# Go image builds use the repository root as their context so modules can
# resolve their `replace` targets under libs/ (see apps/detection-engine/
# Dockerfile). Exclude everything, then re-admit only what a build needs —
# an allowlist keeps an unrelated new directory from silently bloating the
# context or landing in an image layer.
*
!apps
!libs

# Nothing heavy from apps/: the frontend and its dependencies are built by
# their own toolchain, never by a Go image build.
apps/web-ui
**/node_modules
**/.svelte-kit

# Locally built binaries, caches and test artifacts (gitignored, but a dirty
# working tree must not change what a build produces).
**/*.test
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.pcap
**/*.pcapng
apps/detection-engine/detection-engine
apps/device-inventory/device-inventory
apps/killswitch-controller/killswitch-controller
apps/threat-intel-sync/threat-intel-sync
